  "note": "紅茶の雑学 #6: no fixed legal definition; in cafés a tea latte = strongly brewed tea + steamed milk (lots) + milk foam on top, the tea version of a caffè latte (latte = Italian for milk); milk tea = brewed tea with a little milk added afterwards, tea is the star. Starbucks tea latte ≈ half hot water / half milk. Readings: 淹れた→いれた, 濃く→こく, 牛乳→ぎゅうにゅう.",
  "sources": [
    "macaro-ni.jp/178148 (Kirin 午後の紅茶 TEA LATTE): a tea latte pairs strongly brewed tea with milk like a café latte; uses about twice the leaves of 午後の紅茶 ミルクティー; tea flavour stays, clean finish vs milk tea's soft sweetness",
    "walkerplus.com/article/1173769 (Starbucks): tea latte = tea extracted with hot water + steamed milk (steamed with air for a soft mouthfeel, milk sweetness), finished with foamed milk on top",
